description: 'Distilled student on dozken''s architecture at hidden 128 (225,922 params)
  -- v023''s exact recipe, with the DISTILLATION TERM REWEIGHTED towards the teacher''s
  tail. Nothing else changes: same teacher, same hidden size, same loss elsewhere,
  same schedule, same seed.'
hypothesis: 'The teacher term is currently weighted by the metric weight abs(clip(y)),
  which already favours large-abs(y) rows but does so only LINEARLY and only via the
  LABEL. The metric is extraordinarily tail-concentrated (measured: the top 0.5% of
  scored rows hold 11.8% of sum abs(y), the top 5% hold 69.6%), so if the teacher''s
  advantage lives in its extremes then a term weighted by abs(clip(teacher)) should
  transfer MORE of it than a term weighted by abs(y). Prediction: a real gain over
  v023 on identical rows. The prior here is genuinely uncertain -- this could equally
  be a wash, because the metric is a correlation and reweighting between rows mostly
  re-weights WHICH correlation is estimated rather than improving any of them. A wash
  would be informative: it would say teacher weighting is saturated and the remaining
  gap to the leaderboard is not a loss-shaping problem at all.'
change_vs_parent: 'Adds loss.distill_tail_gamma = 2.0 and nothing else. gamma=0 reproduces
  v023 bit-identically (verified: loss diff 0.00e+00, both with and without the distill
  term active), so this isolates the weighting and nothing else.'
